{
  "name": "How to Navigate Property Restoration After Damage",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Navigating property restoration after damage might seem complex, but breaking it down into clear steps can help. Here’s a typical timeline of what happens: Phase 1: Initial Response & Assessment. This usually happens within 24-48 hours for urgent situations. A professional team like HH Remodeling LLC will inspect the damage, identify immediate safety concerns, and document everything. Phase 2: Emergency Mitigation. This phase is all about preventing further damage. Think water extraction, structural shoring, or boarding up compromised areas. Acting fast here is key to saving you headaches and money later. Phase 3: Documentation & Claims. While mitigation is underway, you’ll work with your restoration company and insurance provider. They'll help you compile all necessary documentation for your claim. Phase 4: Repair & Rebuild. Once mitigation is complete and the claim is processed, the actual repair work begins. This could involve anything from drywall and painting to more extensive structural repairs. Phase 5: Final Verification. Before calling the project complete, a final walkthrough ensures all work meets your expectations and industry standards. We’re here to help you through each of these phases with clear communication and expert care. Get in touch to discuss your specific restoration needs.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
